  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement a new generation of gender-responsive national employment policies, including for youth</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In February 2021, the Government adopted the new National Employment Strategy (NES, 2021-2026) and its action plan.

The NES proposes both demand and supply side measures. It contains measures to tackle the specific labour market disadvantage of women, persons with disabilities, people receiving social assistance, and the Roma population. During the second half of 2020, a tripartite multi-ministerial working group relied on the technical assistance of the ILO and of a team of national experts to conduct an ex-post assessment of the previous strategy, the functional review the implementation and coordination capacities of the ministry in charge of labour and of the National Employment Service, and formulate the NES, 2021-2026. At the request of the Ministry and given the emphasis in the NES on the specific labour market challenges faced by young people, the ILO prepared a feasibility assessment concerning the design and implementation of a youth guarantee in Serbia. 

The work with the Ministry and the public employment services on preparing the ground for the youth guarantee relied significantly on the ILO&apos;s facilitation of peer-learning and triangular cooperation with other public employment services (SSTC).   

In the last quarter of 2021, as part of the implementation of the NES Action Plan, the ILO provided technical assistance to the Ministry and the social partners in conducting an analysis of the impacts of a progressive tax on labour.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1. Number of member States with new generation of national employment policies addressing country-specific future of work challenges</narrative>
    </title>
